Just notes for next Changes!

Basically, the idea if to change the current parsing system! And by doing that, it allows for multiple changes throughout the whole project!

First of... I need to disassemble the current parsing method and also the command system!
Making use of the Visitor pattern allows for a much greater range of possibilities...

The parsing system will now consist of "stages"
 - First, conversion of file into bytes!
 - Secondly, creation of class to convert bytes into characters
 - Third step, creation of a class "tokenizer" which creates tokens out of characters
 - Fourth step, parsing system, transforming tokens into fully fledged commands and/or full instructions
 - Lastly, create an "interpreter" which will connect all the inputs and outputs between all classes/stages

* IMPORTANT: All of this process must be made with the use of sequences (lazy)

Regarding the commands itself... remove the execute() function from them and create an accept() function...
This allows for all execution commands to be handled in a single "machine" which will also take care of the memory and instruction process...
This visitor pattern allows us to make more functionalities for the commands, since if we wanted to... we could use the instructions to create a better formatted instruction set...
It allows for many opportunities!